<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Joginder Sen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1904–1986</span> · Also known as Joginder Sen Bahadur</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Joginder Sen was the last ruling raja of Mandi, a princely state in the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/himalayas">Himalaya</a>, from 1913 until it merged into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/himachal-pradesh">Himachal Pradesh</a> in 1948. His reign saw the building of the Shanan hydroelectric power station, opened in 1932, one of the earliest in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, and the town of Jogindernagar is named after him. He later served independent India in public life.</p></div>
